1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Şareb in, gundê me yê xweş, hûn firnê me dibînin.
 
We are in Shareb, our beautiful village, you can see our
bakery.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Naha niha kî berya me nanê tiştî xêr xwar...
 
Now, whoever before us ate bread filled with blessings...

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Tiştekî hewce ye welleh. Firnê we li vir di nav gund da ye.
 
It's a necessary thing, by God. Your bakery is here in the
village.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Navê te çi ye, Mihemed?
 
What is your name, Mihemed?

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Mihemed e.
 
It is Mihemed.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Mihemed.
 
Mihemed.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Nanê we sibehê zû tê hazirkirin, wextê sibehê zû nanê germ
çi xweş e.
 
Your bread is prepared early in the morning, how nice warm
bread is in the early morning.

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Welleh tam e wisa.
 
By God it's tasty like that.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Welleh tam e, we dît? Tu ji kîjan gundî yî xalo?
 
By God it's tasty, you see? Which village are you from
uncle?

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Gundê Çelekiyan.
 
Village of Chelekiyan.

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Gundê Çelekiyan e, malava...
 
It is the village of Chelekiyan, bless your home...

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Dembaş temaşevanên me yên hêja, temaşevanên me yên ezîz.
 
Good day our precious viewers, our dear viewers.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Ez bi hêvî me hûn di nav xêr û xweşiyê da bin, sibehên we bi
xêr.
 
I hope you are in goodness and happiness, good morning to
you.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Hûn çawa ne? Înşallah hûn rind in û rehet in.
 
How are you? God willing you are fine and comfortable.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Îro me berê xwe da ye navçeya Şareba, em ê derbasî Şarebê
bin.
 
Today we have turned our direction to the district of
Shareba, we will pass through Shareb.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Em ê îro werin ji Şarebê suhbetê bikin, derbasî çarşiyê bin.
 
Today we will come to chat in Shareb, and pass through the
market.

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Firnek li Şarebê heye, em çend deqeyan bûn mêvanê nanê wê
firnê.
 
There is a bakery in Shareb, we were guests of the bread of
that bakery for a few minutes.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Em derbasî firnê bûn, firnê me li wir dît. Me çend dîmenên
Şarebê girtin.
 
We passed by the bakery, we saw the bakery there. We took a
few shots of Shareb.

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Lê em ê niha dest pê bikin, em ê nêzîk derbasî Xirabê bin.
 
But we will start now, we will pass closely to Xirabê.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Xirabê jî navçeyekî li kêleka Şarebê ye.
 
Xirabê is also a district next to Shareb.

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Lê îro roja çarşemê ye, li Xirabê bazar jî heye. Em ê çend
dîmenên bazarê jî bigirin.
 
But today is Wednesday, there is also a market in Xirabê. We
will take a few shots of the market as well.

22
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Û bi hev re em ê rojên xweş û kubar li vir derbas bikin.
 
And together we will spend beautiful and nice days here.

23
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Silavên min ji navçeya Şarebê, ji gundê Xirabê re.
 
My greetings to the district of Shareb, to the village of
Xirabê.

24
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Û her kesên li xerîbiyê, yên ku cîh û warê xwe hiştine û
çûne, bila werin ser cîh û warên xwe.
 
And to everyone in exile, those who have left their homes
and places and gone, let them return to their homes and
places.

25
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Heta wê rojê, bi hêvî me em hev bibînin, we vedixwînim em bi
hev re derbasî Şarebê bin.
 
Until that day, I hope we see each other, I invite you to
pass through Shareb together.

26
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Yallah abuy, yallah axuy, yallah eynî!
 
Come on my father, come on my brother, come on my eyes!

27
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Erzan e, erzan e, çi tişt dixwazî bibî, tişt çi dixwazî bibî
xatûna min.
 
It is cheap, it is cheap, take whatever you want, take
whatever you want, my lady.

28
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja, niha jî em li bazarê ne, ev
bazar roja çarşemê tê çêkirin.
 
Yes our precious viewers, now we are also at the market,
this market is set up on Wednesday.

29
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Li Xirabê Şareba... Gundê Şareba û gundên derdorê hemî tên
vê bazarê.
 
In Xirabe Shareba... The village of Shareba and all
surrounding villages come to this market.

30
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Tiştên pêwîstiya xwe ji vê bazarê dibin. Niha jî em dixwazin
di nav bazarê de derbas bin. Piştî wê em ê bi hev re derbasî
nav Şarebê bin.
 
They take their necessities from this market. Now we want to
pass through the market. After that, together we will pass
into Shareb.

31
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Teşkîla xudre û fawakî! Teşkîla xudre... yallah abuy!
 
Assortment of vegetables and fruits! Assortment of
vegetables... come on my father!

32
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Yallah, yallah fadal abuy fadal!
 
Come on, come on go ahead father, go ahead!

33
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Fadal abuy fadal, ehlen we sehlen fadal abuy fadal!
 
Go ahead father go ahead, welcome go ahead father go ahead!

34
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Erzan e ev xudre ha, kîloyek bi pênc hezarî...
 
It's cheap, this vegetable here, a kilo for five thousand...

35
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Em her roj li bazara Şarebê ne, em kar û barên xwe dikin, em
di nav gundî û bajaran de digerin.
 
We are at the Shareb market every day, we do our jobs, we
wander among the villagers and cities.

36
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Erzan e, erzan e, erzan e! Kîlo bi pênc hezarî, bacanê
sor...
 
It is cheap, it is cheap, it is cheap! A kilo for five
thousand, tomatoes...

37
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Bacanê sor kîlo bi pênc hezaran e, tiştên di qedera wê de..
 
Tomatoes a kilo is five thousand, things of its worth..

38
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Bacanê sor bi deh wereqan e! Goceyan bidin, deh wereqe ne!
 
Red tomatoes for ten bills! Give the tomatoes, they are ten
bills!

39
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Îsotê meqdûs, bacanê meqdûs, dido bi pêncan e!
 
Peppers for makdous, eggplants for makdous, two for five!

40
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Erzan e, fîlçe... Pak e, eciq e. Kîloyek pênc wereqe, pênc
hezar e!
 
It is cheap, brush... It is clean and neat. A kilo is five
bills, five thousand!

41
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Ehlen we sehlen ya cemaet, de kerem kin. Şa bin, temam cîh
ye.
 
Welcome oh community, come on in. Be happy, the place is
fine.

42
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Gî firokê me ne, gî xelkê dikanê me ne.
 
They are our sellers, they are all the people of our shop.

43
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Yekî xwest em broka xwe bidin, broka me gî tê.
 
Someone wanted us to give our broccoli, our broccoli all
comes.

44
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Firotina me marûf e.. çi firotî rind e. Çend dixwaze bibe.
 
Our selling is known.. what you sell is good. Take as much
as you want.

45
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Rind e, eger rind be çi dixwaze bibe.
 
It is good, if it is good take whatever you want.

46
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Ehlen we sehlen kekê min, ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome my brother, welcome.

47
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Bêje xalê min çi hewcedariya te heye tu bêje, em di xizmetê
de ne.
 
Tell me my uncle, whatever need you have, tell us, we are at
your service.

48
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Xiyar, xiyar, xiyar!
 
Cucumbers, cucumbers, cucumbers!

49
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Yallah abuy, yallah..
 
Come on my father, come on..

50
00:05:52,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Ruxsat xudre, ruxsat fawakî! Teşkîl xudre, teşkîl fawakî!
 
Cheap vegetables, cheap fruits! Assortment of vegetables,
assortment of fruits!

51
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Vaye bacanê sor e. Vaye xiyar e. Dîna xwe bidê.
 
Here are red tomatoes. Here are cucumbers. Take a look.

52
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Fawakî, xudre, fawakî, xudre!
 
Fruits, vegetables, fruits, vegetables!

53
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Fawakî, xudre, fawakî, xudre!
 
Fruits, vegetables, fruits, vegetables!

54
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Xiyar de he, kîlo de he..
 
There is cucumber, kilo is here..

55
00:06:40,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Ruxsat xudre.. yallah yallah şebab, yallah exuy, yallah
eynî!
 
Cheap vegetables.. come on, come on youth, come on brother,
come on my eyes!

56
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Yallah abuy, yallah eynî, yallah abuy..
 
Come on father, come on my eyes, come on father..

57
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Yallah, fîya.. palas palas palas!
 
Come on, price.. practically free, practically free,
practically free!

58
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Ya şebab, ya welad, kîlo bi dehe! Bacanê sor kîlo bi dehe,
xiyar teze kîlo bi dehe!
 
Oh youth, oh boys, a kilo for ten! Red tomatoes a kilo for
ten, fresh cucumber a kilo for ten!

59
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Tiriya, tiriya kîlo bi dehe! Bacanê sor kîlo bi dehe! Xiyar
teze kîlo bi dehe!
 
Grapes, grapes, a kilo for ten! Red tomatoes a kilo for ten!
Fresh cucumber a kilo for ten!

60
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Xiyar, xiyar, bacanê, xiyar! Xiyar teze kîlo bi dehe!
 
Cucumber, cucumber, tomatoes, cucumber! Fresh cucumber a
kilo for ten!

61
00:07:44,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Bacanê reş, bacanê sor, kîlo bi dehe!
 
Black eggplants, red tomatoes, a kilo for ten!

62
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Demên te xweş bin.
 
May your times be pleasant.

63
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Tu çawa yî, baş î?
 
How are you, are you well?

64
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Elhemdulillah, sax bî.
 
Praise be to God, may you be healthy.

65
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Em bi kêf û xweş bûn... di vê rojê da... em niha li bazara
Xirabê Şarebê amade ne.
 
We were happy and joyful... on this day... we are now
present in the Xirabe market of Shareb.

66
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Em digeriyan, min xwest ez pirs bikim xeber bidim ji te re,
tu ji min re bibêjî ser bazarê.. tişt çawa ne li bazarê..
millet tiştan dikirin nakirin..
 
We were walking around, I wanted to ask and talk to you, for
you to tell me about the market.. how are things in the
market.. are people buying things or not..

67
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Wellehî bi nîsbeta sûkê û bazarê ra, pir tişt erzan in..
Hewayê xelkê dorgirêdayî ma ye, perê di dest milet de tune
ye.
 
By God in relation to the market and bazaar, many things are
cheap.. The situation of the local people remained tied,
there is no money in the hands of the people.

68
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Havê gundan e dor û ber me ne, nêzîk in. Havaya wan rind in.
 
It is the people of the villages around us, they are close.
Their situation is good.

69
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Lê niha wekî mînak, kîlok tiştê wek firingî pênc wereqe ne..
ev jî erzan e.
 
But now for example, a kilo of something like tomatoes is
five bills.. this is also cheap.

70
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Elhemdulillah, millet giş kêfxweş e bi vê erzanî yê.
 
Praise be to God, the people are all happy with this
cheapness.

71
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Em dixwazin ji te bipirsin xalê min, tu ji derveyî vê yekê
li bazarê çi dikî? Tu çi diçînî? Xudre difroşî..
 
We want to ask you my uncle, what do you do in the market
besides this? What do you plant? Selling vegetables..

72
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Ez ji gundê Xelkiya me. Zêdetirî bîst û pênc sal e ez li vê
derê me, ez wisa difroşim.
 
I am from the village of Xelkiya. I have been here for more
than twenty-five years, selling like this.

73
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Em her roj naçin firotinê, em tên vir firotinê dikin.
 
We do not go selling every day, we come here to sell.

74
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Te çi firot îro? Zêde xudre yan fîqiyan..
 
What did you sell today? Mostly vegetables or fruits..

75
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Na tenê em tiştên weha yên rojane difroşin...
 
No, we only sell such daily items...

76
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Baş e.
 
Alright.

77
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Çi tiştê me heye... em difroşin, ez ne firoşkarekî mezin
im...
 
Whatever items we have... we sell them, I am not a big
seller...

78
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Em spasiya we dikin..
 
We thank you..

79
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Welcome...

80
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Ez te aciz nakim... lê belê pirsiyarek min heye, ev bazar
çend rojan e, hûn çend roj tê de dimînin...
 
I won't bother you... but I have a question, how many days
is this market, how many days do you stay in it...

81
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Bi giştî ev bazar rojekê ye... û wekî dîtir, xudre kê
bixwaze bifiroşe dikare.
 
Generally this market is for one day... and otherwise,
whoever wants to sell vegetables can.

82
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Yanî gava bazar çêdibe em tên..
 
Meaning when the market is set up we come..

83
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Ka evê ha giş bi matorê ye, yan mesarîfê wê hawa ye ne?
 
Tell me, is all this by motorcycle, or are its expenses like
this?

84
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Tê bêjî wusa ji ê... welleh ne rahet e.
 
You could say it like this... by God, it's not comfortable.

85
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Weha da rind e, we da hûn cêba xwe perê nadin...
 
In that case it's good, in that case you don't pay money
from your pocket...

86
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Na, elhemdulelah...
 
No, praise be to God...

87
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Û çikê we heyî malê hene, ê jin e, mêr e, kûçik e... rind e.
 
And what household assets do you have, women, men, dogs...
it's good.

88
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Madiyê feqîra bazo.
 
The poor man's livelihood, Bazo.

89
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Belê, madiyê feqîra bazo.
 
Yes, the poor man's livelihood, Bazo.

90
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Belê madiyê feqîra, niha kî feqîr heye, here Efrîn, here
kude, niha tu tiştekî bikirî... dê bibe hezar, dused, sed,
pêncî lê bibe... kera te tiştek bibe...
 
Yes, the poor man's livelihood, now who is poor, go to
Afrin, go anywhere, now if you buy something... it will be a
thousand, two hundred, a hundred, fifty added to it... your
donkey might carry something...

91
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Em kanin bibêjin li gundên derdor, Şera ji, gel derdora
me... li vir hazir dibin.
 
We can say in the surrounding villages, Shera too, the
people of our surroundings... are present here.

92
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Erê, gel vir hazir dibin.
 
Yes, they are present here.

93
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Metîno, gundê Ele Qes, Sînko, Şero, Çemo, giş l' dor in, l'
derdorê me ne...
 
Metino, the village of Ele Qes, Sinko, Sero, Chemo, all are
around, they are in our surroundings...

94
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Ev gundên derdorê me ne... Ew nêzîk l' ba me ne.
 
These are our surrounding villages... They are close to us.

95
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Wextê wekî Efrîn vebû, seyare nedibûn, û bazara Efrîn l' vir
jî tê çêkirin.
 
When Afrin opened, there were no cars, and the market of
Afrin is also held here.

96
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Erê, roja Çarşemê noka bazara Efrînê ye, min bîst yek e,
yekî wê, roja Pêncşemê ye.
 
Yes, on Wednesday is now the market of Afrin, I heard it is
the first, its first is on Thursday.

97
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Pêncşemê ji ya Ba'dîna ye...
 
Thursday is also Ba'dina's market...

98
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Êh, ê Ba'dîna.
 
Yeah, Ba'dina's.

99
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Em spasiya we dikin, em pir kêfxweş bûn.
 
We thank you, we were very pleased.

100
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Sax bin... ehlen we sehlen...
 
Be healthy... welcome...

101
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Merheba ciwano, em hê ro li bazara Şera ne.
 
Hello youngsters, today we are in the market of Shera.

102
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Navê min Îbrahîm e, Îbrahîm, ez ji Şera me.
 
My name is Ibrahim, Ibrahim, I am from Shera.

103
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Roja Çarşemê bazar çêdibe, xudre tên, fawake tên, mûnet tên,
malat tên...
 
On Wednesdays the market happens, vegetables come, fruits
come, supplies come, goods come...

104
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Ji çil gundî tên... ji nahîye Şera gî tên. Meselen, xudrî
xwe dikirin, fawakî dikirin, mûnetê malê dikirin...
 
They come from forty villages... they all come from the
Shera sub-district. For example, they buy their vegetables,
they buy their fruits, they buy their household supplies...

105
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Wekî hûn dibînin, munazîfat heye, yanî gî tişt heye.
 
As you can see, there are detergents, meaning there's
everything.

106
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Û hefteyê carekê bazar çêdibe, roja Çarşemê çêdibe.
 
And the market takes place once a week, it happens on
Wednesday.

107
00:11:52,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Û tabî hûn gî pê zanin, û saat we xweş.
 
And of course you all know about it, and have a good time.

108
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Fere dûr kîloyek bi deh hezara!
 
Tomatoes, one kilo for 10 thousand!

109
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Kîloyek tirşiyê heşt hezara!
 
One kilo of pickles for 8 thousand!

110
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Fere dûr deh hezara!
 
Tomatoes 10 thousand!

111
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Bîst û pênc ho... bîst û pênc... bîber...
 
Twenty-five oh... twenty-five... peppers...

112
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Bacanê reş kîlo bi deh hezara!
 
Eggplants, one kilo for 10 thousand!

113
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Kîloyek xiyar bi deh hezara!
 
One kilo of cucumbers for 10 thousand!

114
00:12:40,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Sêvê sor... sêvê sor... kîlo bi bîst û pênc hezara!
 
Red apples... red apples... one kilo for 25 thousand!

115
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Belê temaşevanên me yê hêja, naha jî em li ber firnê ne.
 
Yes our dear viewers, now we are also in front of the
bakery.

116
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Ev firne jî, ez biçûk bûm tê bîra min, gundên hawîrdor pir
dihatin vir nan dikirin.
 
This bakery as well, I remember when I was young, many from
the surrounding villages would come here and buy bread.

117
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Nan pir dihatin sekinandin, de bera em biçûk bûn, me
makîneyên xwe li vir disekinandin û em dihatin dorê
disekinîn.
 
Much bread was waited for, back when we were little, we
would park our vehicles here and we would come stand in
line.

118
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Em dihatin aliyê firnê.
 
We used to come to the side of the bakery.

119
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
L' wextê, me ji vê firnê nan dibir, nanê wê jî tenik û spî
ye.
 
At that time, we would take bread from this bakery, its
bread is thin and white.

120
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Yanî kêfa mirov jê re tê, te destê xwe kiratê da te bixwara.
 
I mean it gives a person joy, if you reach your hand in to
eat it.

121
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Lê naha jî bi me re bin, emê bi hevre derbasî firnê bibin.
 
But now stay with us, we will enter the bakery together.

122
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Em kanin bibêjin... l' Şera xeynî wê yek firne nine.
 
We can say... there is no other bakery in Shera except for
this one.

123
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Beriya bi deh, şeş - heft sala, em jî bi xwera keti bûn,
derbasî firnê bûn...
 
Before, 10, 6-7 years ago, we also got into this with
ourselves, we entered the bakery...

124
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Ez biçûk bûm tê bîra min.
 
I was small, I remember.

125
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Lê naha emê bi hev re derbas bibin... a l'hundir ve...
 
But now we will enter together... to the inside...

126
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
hinekî hûn ê l' vir bibînin...
 
you will see a little here...

127
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Em ê nanê xwe bibînin, weke berê ye... an naha hatiye
guherandin.
 
We will see our bread, is it like before... or has it been
changed now.

128
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Bi me re bin, em ê naha bi hev re derbas bibin.
 
Stay with us, we will enter together now.

129
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Temaşevanên me yê hêja... bêhna nan... bêhna vê nanê xweş
e...
 
Our dear viewers... the smell of bread... the smell of this
bread is nice...

130
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Ez bi hêvî me înşallah her kesek bixwe û têr bixwe...
 
I hope, God willing, everyone eats and eats their fill...

131
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Gundên derdorê Şera, em kanin bibêjin derbasî Şera dibin.
 
The villages around Shera, we can say they pass through
Shera.

132
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Û tên nanê xwe ji vê firnê dibirin.
 
And they come and take their bread from this bakery.

133
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Nan wekî berê ye, nehatiye guherandin.
 
The bread is like before, it hasn't been changed.

134
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Lê tiştekî xweş l' vê firnê da em dibînin...
 
But a nice thing about this bakery we see here...

135
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Ev tişto jî, naha em kanin bêjin em nanê xwe gîş amade
dikin, hazir e...
 
This thing as well, now we can say we prepare all our bread,
it's ready...

136
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Hazir û bi rehetî tê cizda yê...
 
Ready and easily it goes into the bag...

137
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Lê tiştekî xweş l' vê firnê... em kanin bibêjin... hûn l'
vir dibînin...
 
But a nice thing about this bakery... we can say... you see
it here...

138
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Bêhna nanê xwe didin... da tu kanî nanê xwe l' vir raxê...
 
They let the bread give its smell... so you can lay out your
bread here...

139
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Tê raxê... piştî ko hinekî sar bike, tê têxe kîsê.
 
You lay it out... after it cools down a bit, you put it in
the bag.

140
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Wê manê, nanê me zû nedişkest, zû nedibû hevîr.
 
That means, our bread wouldn't break quickly, it wouldn't
quickly become doughy.

141
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Maşelleh nanê xwe jî pak e...
 
Mashallah, its bread is also clean...

142
00:15:51,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Em naha nanê xwazin... û em naha ê ra bixwin.
 
We want bread now... and now we will eat it.

143
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Tu kanî bibînî wê, naha rast e sar bû...
 
You can see it, it is really cold now...

144
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Sar bû.
 
It cooled down.

145
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Ev nan, tewr demdirêj dimîne... na dibe hevîr...
 
This bread stays for a very long time... it does not become
dough...

146
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Lê naha em bi rehetî cêza dîn in...
 
But now we with comfort put it in the bag...

147
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Lê ji her malekê jî... em kanin bibêjin... kesek sibê zu
radibû diçû nan dibir...
 
But from every house too... we can say... someone would wake
up early in the morning and go get bread...

148
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Radikir dorê li ber firnê.
 
They would wait in line in front of the bakery.

149
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Lê ev tişto niha kêm bûn e... Lê em bi hêvî ne ev tişt di
nav me ra winda nebin. Em miletê Efrînê, ev tişt l' cem me
kevnar e.
 
But these things have become fewer now... But we hope this
thing doesn't disappear from among us. We, the people of
Afrin, these things are ancient to us.

150
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Di ziyaretan da em kanin bibêjin... ev tişt l' cem me pir
kevnare...
 
In visitations we can say... these things among us are very
ancient...

151
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Lê vê firnê jî, me xwest darbazî bîn... û hinek ji we ra
biseh kin...
 
But this bakery too, we wanted to enter... and show it a bit
to you...

152
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Wextê ez biçûk bûm, em dihatin vê firnê, bîranînê l' vir
hene...
 
When I was young, we would come to this bakery, there are
memories here...

153
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Û ka kî ji me mezin bû, kî ji, di vê firnê ra hatî derbas
bûye...
 
And well, whoever of us has grown up, whoever has come and
passed through this bakery...

154
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Ji kîjan gundê derdor, ew jî l' vê firnê nanê xwe kiriye...
 
From whichever surrounding village, they also bought their
bread at this bakery...

155
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Maxwas bi radbûn
 
The early risers used to wake up

156
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Dengê dîkan rêşad bûn
 
The sound of roosters brought joy

157
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Xizan, asî bi radbûn
 
The poor and rebellious used to wake up

158
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Her kes bi kar û şixwê xwe bûn
 
Everyone was at their chores and work

159
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Pîs û qeşmer tê kêm bûn
 
The bad and the clowns were scarce

160
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Bi ken û xweş, rewan bûn
 
With smiles and goodness, they flowed

161
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Şivan, û kar, û berx kin
 
The shepherd, the labor, and the lambs

162
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Heval bûn, xwişk û b'ra bûn
 
Were friends, were sisters and brothers

163
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Tev zengilê raman bûn
 
They were all the bells of thought

164
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Rojên gundê me,
 
The days of our village,

165
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Hîn ber çavê min.
 
Are still before my eyes.

166
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Şevên gundê me,
 
The nights of our village,

167
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Nanê genim, ê tenûr da...
 
The wheat bread, from the tandoor...

168
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Dûxana wê şîn dibû ro...
 
Its smoke turned blue to the sun...

169
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Digerî wê l'xeyala...
 
It wanders there in the thoughts...

170
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Digerî l'ser... pûzekî...
 
It wanders on... a peak...

171
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Dest me dabû... hev çilokan...
 
We had held... hands on the branches...

172
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Çivîkan didan, av û av...
 
The birds gave, water and water...

173
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Me bi hev dixwar, wecê nan û rêzê...
 
We ate together, the meal of bread and grapes...

174
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Hîn l' bîra min!
 
I still remember!

175
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Rojên gundê me,
 
The days of our village,

176
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Hîn ber çavê min.
 
Are still before my eyes.

177
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Dengê xwandinê, a zarokan...
 
The sound of reading, of the children...

178
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Ji mektebê, nava gund da radikî...
 
From the school, it rose in the village...

179
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Pêşê camiyê pîş dar bûn...
 
In front of the mosque, they were craftsmen...

180
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Denge rûş û kal e gund...
 
The voices of the youth and elders of the village...

181
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Dixemlîn mal û zeviyan...
 
They decorated the homes and fields...

182
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Digerin, raqs û dîlan...
 
They wander, dance and circles...

183
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Gund dilerzandin, qîz û xortan...
 
The girls and boys made the village tremble...

184
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Şevên sef d' bûn sînem...
 
The nights aligned, became a cinema...

185
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Hîn tê bîra min!
 
I still remember!

186
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Ev rojên me,
 
These days of ours,

187
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Narê ji bîra min,
 
Don't leave my mind,

188
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Zaroktiya min!
 
My childhood!

189
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Hev lîstinê hev agir...
 
Playing together, fire together...

190
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Em lîstin da bi qîr e...
 
We played with shouts...

191
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Seyarê tehtî b'çelak e...
 
The wooden car in the mud...

192
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Çavşarkê li deriyan e...
 
Hide and seek at the doors...

193
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Di malên kevirî da...
 
In the stone houses...

194
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Xeyalên me da di firî...
 
Flew within our dreams...

195
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Nedibû qet nav vî da...
 
It never happened within this...

196
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Vî halê min...
 
This condition of mine...

197
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Hatiya di bîra min da...
 
It came into my memory...

198
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Belê temaşevanê me yê hêja, naha jî em li çarşiyê, Şera ne.
 
Yes, our esteemed viewers, now we are at the market of
Shera.

199
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Sûkê Şera... em kanin bibêjin...
 
The market of Shera... we can say...

200
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Naha mevsima zeytûna hatiye, wey mevsima zeytûnê çi xwaş e
li Şera...
 
Now the olive season has come, oh how nice the olive season
is in Shera...

201
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Wextê em ji zeytûna d'hatin, em d' gundî ra darbas bûn...
 
When we used to come from the olives, we passed through the
village...

202
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Di wî gundî muşebek çêdikirin.
 
In that village they were making mushabak.

203
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Bîhnê wî muşebekî pir xwaş d'bû, wa rojê pir xwaş bû.
 
The smell of that mushabak was very nice, those days were
very nice.

204
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Lê em j' tiştin d'bihêvî ne... kû wî rojê vegere di Şera...
em yê dîsa di Efrînê bibin... am dîsa darbas b'in ba hev
ra...
 
But we are hopeful of things... that those days return to
Shera... we will be in Afrin again... we will pass by
together again...

205
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Em naha ba hev ra...
 
We now together...

206
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Siba te ba xêr.
 
Good morning.

207
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
B'xêr û b'selamet.
 
Welcome and safely.

208
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Saet a te xwaşbî.
 
May your time be good.

209
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Û tu ji sax bî.
 
And you too, be healthy.

210
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Wekî destpêk em ji derbasbûyîna me di navenda Şera, ya ku ev
tişt tajî berî em biçin gundên derdorê me, em têne cem kekê.
 
As a start, during our passing through the center of Shara,
since these things are fresh before we go to our surrounding
villages, we come to this brother.

211
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Em dixwazin em pê re biaxivin.
 
We want to talk to him.

212
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Bi xêr hatî bernameya me.
 
Welcome to our program.

213
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Kerem ke.
 
You are welcome.

214
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Navê te bi xêr?
 
What is your good name?

215
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Navê min Zekeriya ye.
 
My name is Zekeriya.

216
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Kekê Zekeriya, tu bi xwe ji Şera yî, lê tu li Şera kar dikî?
 
Brother Zekeriya, you yourself are from Shara, and you work
in Shara?

217
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Temam, erê.
 
Yes, exactly.

218
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Tu mişebekê çêdikî.
 
You make mushabak.

219
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Erê, teqîd, sax bî.
 
Yes, exactly, stay healthy.

220
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Tu ji kengî ve di vî karî de yî?
 
Since when have you been in this work?

221
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Welleh ez li Libnanê hînî mişebekê bûme.
 
Well, I learned mushabak in Lebanon.

222
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Lê hiliwiyat ji Helebê.
 
But sweets from Aleppo.

223
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Te hiliwiyat jî heye, an mişebek bi tenê?
 
Do you have sweets as well, or just mushabak?

224
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Hiliwiyat jî heye, lê mişebek min li Libnanê hîn bûme.
 
There are sweets too, but I learned mushabak in Lebanon.

225
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Mişebek di zeytûnan da xweş dibe, sedema wê çi ye? Te kengî
dest pê kir, te j' min ra negot...
 
Mushabak becomes delicious during the olive season, what is
the reason for that? When did you start, you didn't tell
me...

226
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Welleh dema...
 
Well, when...

227
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Ew jî wekî mewsim e keko, ji baran, rehmet barî, êdî
zivistan şîrînî xweş dibe.
 
It's also a season, brother, when rain and mercy fall, in
winter sweets become delicious.

228
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Tê bîra min wextê, berê, wextê em çûn zeytûnan jî...
 
I remember back in the day, when we went for olives too...

229
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Her însanek Efrînî diçû zeytûnan...
 
Every person from Afrin who went for olives...

230
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Ekîd, teb'en.
 
Definitely, of course.

231
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Dema ku diqediya, zeytûn didan, em dihatin...
 
When it was finished, dropping off the olives, we would
come...

232
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Em çûne cem, diviyabû em mişebekê bistînin, an me xwarin
dikiriya.
 
We would go, we had to buy mushabak, or we bought food.

233
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Ew tehma wê mişebekê çiqas xweş e!
 
The taste of that mushabak is so delicious!

234
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Erê, em ê tam bikin û hûn ê jî bibînin ha.
 
Yes, we will taste it and you will see it too.

235
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
Em ê waqi'ê bibînin...
 
We will see the reality...

236
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Û ji berê de jî mişebek xelastek e, bi şeklekî giştî...
însanê karkerên feqîr dema daxwazin mişebekê bixwin...
 
And since the past mushabak is a treat, in general... when
the poor working people want to eat mushabak...

237
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Dema xelas dikin, divê mişebekê bixwin. Xelastek e, anku
şerta amale ye.
 
When they finish, they have to eat mushabak. It's a treat,
meaning the condition for the workers.

238
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Em biçûk bûn, me jî ew tişt dikir.
 
When we were young, we used to do that too.

239
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:19,000
Derbas be... hiliwiyatên te yê din jî ma re hene yan na?
 
Go ahead... do you have other sweets for us or not?

240
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Hiliwiyat, bi penîr halawê bi penîr jî heye.
 
Sweets, we also have cheese halawa.

241
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Halawet cibn e?
 
Is it cheese halawa?

242
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Na, halawa 'adî ye.
 
No, it's regular halawa.

243
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Em tînin, havînê meste, qeşte tînin û havînî em fêkiyan
tînin.
 
We bring it, in the summer we bring yogurt, cream, and in
the summer we bring fruits.

244
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Li gorî mewsima wan e.
 
It depends on their season.

245
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Lê ev mişebek bi taybet wextê zeytûnan pir xweş dibe bi
baranê.
 
But this mushabak is specifically very delicious during the
olive season with the rain.

246
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Û ew rûn, wextê bi rûnê em çêdikin jî...
 
And that oil, when we make it with oil too...

247
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Û bi taybet, yê malên mezin bin, yê zarok têde, xweş dibe.
 
And specifically, those who have big households, with
children in it, it is nice.

248
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Heta yê ku dilê wî diêşe... wekî derman e, dema yek kîloyek
mişebek ji wan re bibe, kêfxweş dibin.
 
Even the one whose stomach hurts... it is like a remedy,
when one brings a kilo of mushabak for them, they become
happy.

249
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Yanî ew şertê jî ev e.
 
Meaning that is the condition.

250
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Bi rastî destên te sax bin kekê.
 
Truly, health to your hands, brother.

251
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Te jî sax be.
 
Health to you too.

252
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Serkeftin bo ciwanan, tu ji Libnanê hatî û te tiştekî wekî
vê çêkiriye.
 
Success to the youth, you came from Lebanon and you made
something like this.

253
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:57,000
Ev şerefeke mezin e ji me re ku tu hemî cihan ji xwe re
dibînî.
 
It is a great honor for us that you can find all places for
yourself.

254
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Temaşevanên me yê hêja... car caran yek di şîroveyan de
dibêje, hûn wî navî dikin, ew mal dikişînin.
 
Our dear viewers... sometimes someone says in the comments,
you name this, you film that house.

255
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Ser navê yekî... her tiştê em dikişînin, ew ne îlan e.
 
On behalf of someone... everything we film, that is not an
advertisement.

256
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Em bi hêvî ne xwediyê me... her firoşgehê, em ê wacibê me ye
em biçin cem wan.
 
We hope that our people... every shop, it is our duty to go
to them.

257
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Û em bi kamerayên xwe, ji wateyên we re, her tişt nîşan
dikin û ne îlan e.
 
And with our cameras, for your sake, we show everything and
it is not an ad.

258
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:22,000
Kesên ku van tiştan dinivîsin ew şîroveyan me dikin.
 
To the people who write these things in the comments for us.

259
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Em spasiya te dikin kekê.
 
We thank you, brother.

260
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Spas bo te, hûn bûne mêhvan.
 
Thanks to you, you have become guests.

261
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Û wekî mêhvan xalê Xidir li ba te rûniştiye.
 
And as a guest, uncle Xidir is sitting near you.

262
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Silav Xidir seet xweş, qe rûne.
 
Greetings Xidir, good health, have a seat.

263
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:32,000
Destê we sax bin, piyan sax bin.
 
Health to your hands, health to your feet.

264
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:35,000
Em ê naha tam bikin...
 
We will taste it now...

265
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:40,000
Em ê tama gundê, ew tama wexta em zeytûnan de... wek berê
ye... an wek niha ye?
 
We will see the taste of the village, that taste of when we
are in the olives... is it like before... or like now?

266
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Înşellah bi îzna Xwedê. Dê xwedê nîşan nede ku em qelpî kin
jî.
 
God willing. May God not show us cheating either.

267
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Bide yê pişt kamerayê jî...
 
Give it to the one behind the camera too...

268
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:52,000
Destê xwe bikişîne... bide yê pişt kamerayê mîna vî rengî.
 
Pull your hand... give it to the one behind the camera like
this.

269
00:22:52,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Bismillah.
 
In the name of God.

270
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Tama wî... tama wî ya yê berê ye, tu guhertin lê tineye.
 
Its taste... its taste is like the old one, there's no
change in it.

271
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Bi îzna Xwedê ye, welleh mêro tiştên esasan dikişînin, zeyta
paqij.
 
By God's permission, really a man uses the basics, clean
oil.

272
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Destên te sax bin kekê qurban.
 
Health to your hands brother, bless you.

273
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Heke mirov siheta xwe, hesaba nekir, mirov zirarê ji xwe re
çêdike.
 
If a person doesn't consider their health, one brings harm
to oneself.

274
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,000
Tu li ser xêrê bî.
 
May you be in goodness.

275
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Seheta te xweş. Hiliwiyat Ebû Nûr.
 
Good health to you. Sweets Abu Nur.

276
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Hiliwiyat Ebû Nûr. Dikaneke hiliwiyat ê wekî hûn dibînin e.
 
Sweets Abu Nur. A sweets shop as you can see.

277
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Spas dikin... em ê ber bi dikanên Şera da, em derbas bin.
Spas.
 
We thank you... we will pass through the shops of Shara.
Thanks.

278
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:53,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

279
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Belê temaşevanên me hêja, em li şarê rastî tiştekî pir xweş
hatin, kekê me.
 
Yes our dear viewers, we came across something very nice in
the city, our brother.

280
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Ji gundî Qotana ye. Piştî heşt salan, xwedê ev lawko daye.
Navê te çi ye?
 
He is from the village of Qotana. After eight years, God has
given him this boy. What is your name?

281
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Mihemed.
 
Mihemed.

282
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,000
Ey qurbana te navê te! Tu li vir difroşî?
 
Oh, I'd be a sacrifice for your name! Do you sell here?

283
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Xwedê te bihêle... Em te nas bikin pismam?
 
May God protect you... Can we know you, cousin?

284
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Serçava xalê... ez ji Efrînê me, navê min Silêman e.
 
On my eyes uncle... I am from Afrin, my name is Silêman.

285
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Çaxê em hatin me... Efrîn, gişt kes, beşdarî kirin.
 
When we came... all the people of Afrin participated.

286
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Welleh Xelîl bistahil e... Milyon, kerem ke!
 
By God Khalil deserves it... A million, you're welcome!

287
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,000
Tu bavê wî yî?
 
Are you his father?

288
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Ez bapîrê wî me.
 
I am his grandfather.

289
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:04,000
Maşellah, maşellah!
 
Mashallah, mashallah!

290
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:08,000
Ev bavê wî ye... Were ammo, were ammo. Ev bavê wî ye.
 
This is his father... Come uncle, come uncle. This is his
father.

291
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Piştî heşt salan Xwedê ev zarok da ye, û we ev wek qurban jê
re çêkiriye.
 
After eight years God gave this child, and you made this as
a sacrifice for him.

292
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Ez ji xwedê hêvî dikim, her kesê bextê wî hebe, ew bibîne.
 
I hope from God, anyone who has luck, sees this.

293
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Me xwast em bîranînekê jê re bihêlin.. sibe ku mezin bibe.
 
We wanted to leave a memory for him... tomorrow when he
grows up.

294
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Sax bî, xwedê emrê te dirêj bike, xwedê te bihêle bo me.
 
Stay healthy, may God lengthen your life, may God keep you
for us.

295
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:28,000
Xwedê wî ji we re bihêle... Ger te daweya wî nekiribe...
 
May God keep him for you... If you haven't done his
celebration (circumcision)...

296
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Bi bîstûyek def'an qeyda we çêdikim?
 
I will do it twenty-one times?

297
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Na... înşellah yek car e...
 
No... God willing it's just once...

298
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:35,000
Siheta we xweş.
 
Good health to you.

299
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,000
Xwedê ji te razî be keko Xelîl, sehet xweş.
 
May God be pleased with you brother Khalil, good health.

300
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Xwedê ji we razî be xalê.
 
May God be pleased with you uncle.

301
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:58,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

302
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Dembaş xalo.
 
Good day uncle.

303
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,000
Roj baş bo te.
 
Good day to you.

304
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Tu çawa yî, siheta te rind e?
 
How are you, is your health good?

305
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:34,000
Elhemdulillah. Xwedê qewetê bide te, siheta te baş e?
 
Praise be to God. May God give you strength, is your health
good?

306
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Em baş in elhemdulillah. Welleh em li dor emr û siheta
xwe...
 
We are well, praise be to God. Well, we are about our age
and health...

307
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Elhemdulillah, şikir welleh ha şeba wilo emr û sihet
elhemdulillah.
 
Praise be to God, thanks, well you know, age and health,
praise be to God.

308
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,000
Em te nas bikin berî her tiştî?
 
Can we get to know you before anything else?

309
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Ez ji gundê Şera me, Nûrî ye Cafer... Malbata me re dibêjin
Mala Hemikê.
 
I am from the village of Shara, I am Nûrî of Ja'far... They
call our family the Hamik House.

310
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,000
Mala Hemikê.
 
The Hamik House.

311
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

312
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Şêst û sê salan emrê te di vî gundî de derbas bûye, hûn
rûniştvanên vî ne?
 
Sixty-three years of your life have passed in this village,
are you residents of it?

313
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Belê asasan em ji gundê Dûrî ne. Em rûbarî ne.
 
Yes originally we are from the village of Dûrî. We are from
the river area.

314
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,000
Derdora rûbarê...
 
Around the river...

315
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Em derbasî nav Şera bûn. Em şerq û nahiye, em dikarin
bêjin...
 
We entered Shara. We can say the east and the district...

316
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Belê, em hinekî dîroka Şera bizanibin...
 
Yes, we want to know a bit about the history of Shara...

317
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Berî ez pirs bikim xalê min, navê Şera ji ku hat?
 
Before I ask my uncle, where did the name Shara come from?

318
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,000
Wateya vî navî ya Şera çiye?
 
What is the meaning of this name Shara?

319
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Welleh wek ku ez zanim... navê Şera, her hal...
 
Well as far as I know... the name Shara, anyway...

320
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Vê hatinê ku ji jêr de û ji jor de hatine li rojhilatê...
 
This coming that came from below and from above to the
east...

321
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Ez dibêjim bi wî navî ye... wek vê wextê navê wê danîn Şera.
 
I say it's by that name... like they gave it the name Shara
at that time.

322
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:27,000
Ez nizanim wilo tê bîra min.
 
I don't know, that's what comes to my mind.

323
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Naha, şera giştî çend mal tê de hene?
 
Now, how many houses are there in Shara overall?

324
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Teqrîben, ji dused û dused û pazdeh, dused û bîst gundî
hene.
 
Approximately, there are from two hundred to two hundred and
fifteen, two hundred and twenty houses.

325
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Û çend malbat hene di vir da jiyan dikin?
 
And how many families are living here?

326
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Welleh bi deqîq asasan ew malbatên mezin...
 
Well exactly essentially those big families...

327
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:49,000
Malê Eliyê Molo... Malê Silo... hene...
 
The family of Eliyê Molo... the family of Silo... are
there...

328
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Malê Hecê Hesen, Malê Mûsil, malê Hec Haşim.
 
The family of Hej Hesen, the family of Mûsil, the family of
Hej Hashim.

329
00:28:54,000 --> 00:29:00,000
Malê Qeremên, malê Hemikê. Malê Qurre... Malê Çûxader...
 
The family of Qeremên, the family of Hemikê. The family of
Qurre... the family of Çûxader...

330
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Malê Heso... Û çend malbatên din jî hene ku em tevlî hev
bûne wekî aşîr têne hesebandin.
 
The family of Heso... And there are a few other families too
that we have mixed together with and are considered a tribe.

331
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Çend malbatên din jî hene ku eslê xwe ji ciyên din hatine,
li vî ciyî hesibî.
 
There are a few other families too that originally came from
other places, and are accounted for here.

332
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Kîjan malin ew ên ku hatine hesibîn?
 
Which families are those that are considered to have come
here?

333
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Koçer in wek mînak... û malê Eglê ne...
 
Nomads for example... and the family of Egle...

334
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Hene, ewe Malê Heskê ne, Malê Înalû ne.
 
There are, those are the family of Heske, the family of
Înalû.

335
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Hene wilo ez nizanim... hene malên dîtir.
 
There are some like that I don't know... there are other
families.

336
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Naha em di rê de dihatin me şikeftek di nav gund da, li jêr
dît.
 
Now we were coming on the road and we saw a cave in the
village, below.

337
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:38,000
Ez dixwazim hinekî derbarê vî şikeftê, ji min re xeberekê
bidî...
 
I want you to tell me a bit of news about this cave...

338
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Gelo ev kevnar e... tu zanebûnekî wê heye...
 
Is this ancient... do you have any knowledge of it...

339
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Şikeft...
 
The cave...

340
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:45,000
Çend sal emrê wê şikeftê heye?
 
How many years old is that cave?

341
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:50,000
Welleh divê şikeft wekî navê xwe kevnar in...
 
Well these caves must be as ancient as their name...

342
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Wek asas em dibêjin wextê berê li jêr, gundê cîran yê
hatine...
 
Basically we say in the old times below, the neighboring
village that came...

343
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:58,000
...wê demê ew şikeft ku bûn e.
 
...at that time those caves existed.

344
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Ez bi xwe nizanim, ez qet nizanim ew çawa bûye.
 
I don't know myself, I don't know at all how it was.

345
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:03,000
Mesele em werin bal koçkêt xweliya min, koçkêt xuya di kir.
 
For example, let's come to the ash pens of mine, did it show
the pens?

346
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:03,000
Sê şirkat li wura hebûn.
 
Yes.

347
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Sê şirkat li wura hebûn.
 
There were three partnerships there.

348
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Yek dîgotin ew malê Elî axa, yek malê Mehmed axa, yek malê
Hesen axa, evna ji gundî yanî jibo vî bûn pismamê hev din e,
 
One they called the flock of Eli Agha, one the flock of
Mehmed Agha, one the flock of Hesen Agha, they were
villagers, meaning for this they were cousins to each other,

349
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:23,000
yanî heta apê me Heşaş hebû wekî sed-sedûpêncî mî xwe hebû
doguya me de kir, şirkat a malê Elî axa
 
meaning even our uncle Hashhash was there, he had about
100-150 sheep of his own, our flock was pastured in the
partnership of Eli Agha's flock.

350
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:28,000
wekî sed biznê malê Me'dîn hebû doguya wan ji dikiro ew
jikî,
 
Like there were 100 goats of Me'din's flock, they pastured
them there too.

351
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

352
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Û hewa din jê ... dewarê gund dikiro. Gundan dewarê gund
dikiro. Te d'vê qantir me hebûn,
 
And the others from... they pastured the village's
livestock. The villages pastured the village's livestock.
Even we had mules,

353
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:43,000
Û paşî wê ew xaneyen qentirme bûn, û paşî we xaneyen jî giş
hetan bi nîvê d'kirin a axê. Yê ji cî kurmiyê va.
 
And then after that those mule stables, and after that all
those houses they would fill up to the middle with dirt.
Also because of their worms.

354
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Heta min pirs d'kir min d'got sebeb çîye hevan heta bi nîvî
de axê danin, digot me'neyek diz ana..
 
Even I used to ask and say what is the reason to fill these
up to the middle with dirt, they would say the reason is
thieves...

355
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Digot diz hene. Û heta dîwarê paşin digot dîrek a d'kero nav
kavran, mehneyek diz weke pêş avêto rastî dîrek wê re.
 
They said there are thieves. And even the back wall they
said they put a pillar inside the stones, the reason is if a
thief opens it and steps forward, he would come across the
pillar.

356
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

357
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:03,000
Em sipasiya te dikin.
 
We thank you.

358
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:10,000
Ê sipasiya wa dikin. Hatina we u xêra we. Û serkeftin j'wa
re inşallah.
 
I thank you. Welcome. And success to you, God willing.

359
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:12,000
Wella serkeftin ji milete mi Kurd teva re
 
By God, success to all of our Kurdish nation.

360
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Amîn ya reb.
 
Amen, O Lord.

361
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Xwedê emrê te dirêj ke xalo
 
May God prolong your life, uncle.

362
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Amîn ya reb.. xwedê emrê we dirêj ke û canê we sax ke û bê
mogiya wa de .. wa b'wada de .. û xwedê cafa wa li boçê
nehêle..
 
Amen, O Lord. May God prolong your lives and keep you
healthy, and in your efforts... and you too... and may God
not let your efforts go to waste...

363
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Amîn. Te emrek hene.. ti gotinek te hene.
 
Amen. Do you have an order... do you have a word?

364
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Welle emrê min.. emrê xwedê ne .. Canê te sax ..
 
By God, my order... is the order of God. Bless you.

365
00:31:56,000 --> 00:32:01,000
Eme zin bûn li vî gundî, her tiştê xweş me lê didît.
 
We grew up in this village, we saw everything beautiful in
it.

366
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Çiqas sal j'emrê me çûn, min nizanî çawa derbas bûn.
 
How many years of our lives passed, I didn't know how they
passed.

367
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Hîn ber çavên min rûyên şêrîn, dikirin jivan wextên şêrîn.
 
Still before my eyes are sweet faces, making sweet times.

368
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Çi xweş bû zemanê paşayî, çîrokên tijî evîn.
 
How beautiful was the time of the past, stories full of
love.

369
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Hîn li bîra min,
 
I still remember,

370
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Şefeqa sibê radibûn,
 
They woke up at dawn,

371
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Dengê dîkan reşad dibûn.
 
The roosters' sound broke the dark.

372
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Azane nasî we bûn,
 
You were free acquaintances,

373
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Herkes kariyê şeva bûn.
 
Everyone went to their night work.

374
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Pê zeytûnan hev ra d'çûn,
 
They went to the olives together,

375
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Bi ken û xweş raw da çûn.
 
With smiles and joy they walked.

376
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Şivana kar u berxên xwe,
 
The shepherd with his kids and lambs,

377
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Hawal bûn xweşk u b'rak bûn.
 
They were friends, sisters and brothers.

378
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:42,000
Hîn li bîra min,
 
I still remember,

379
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Rojên gundê min,
 
The days of my village,

380
00:32:44,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Şevên gundê min.
 
The nights of my village.

381
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Nanê genim yê di tendûr da,
 
Wheat bread in the tandoor,

382
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,000
dimeşîn di rêkên dûr da,
 
walking on the long roads,

383
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Digeriyan na rişas û sir da,
 
Wandering in the snow and cold,

384
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:22,000
wek hesîn pozê zinar ra.
 
like iron on the edge of the rocks.

385
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Dest nedan siqa û çokan,
 
Hands didn't touch the...

386
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:27,000
kefxweşiya qevirkan,
 
the joy of the...

387
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Mewij dikirin vî curnan,
 
They picked from these troughs,

388
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:32,000
çavên milêt te d'geriyan.
 
the eyes of the nation searched for you.

389
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Hîn li bîra min.
 
Still in my memory.

390
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Dengê xwendina xort û qîzan,
 
The sound of the studying of boys and girls,

391
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:39,000
mekteba nav gund dihat.
 
came from the school in the village.

392
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Pêşiyê camî a wa azan,
 
In front of the mosque and its call to prayer,

393
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:44,000
rebrabûn hevdu dibûn bavûkan.
 
they became fathers together.

394
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:46,000
D'xemilîn bi ala zozan,
 
Adorned with the colors of the high pastures,

395
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:49,000
digerîn raqs û dîlan,
 
going around in dance and celebration,

396
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Gund bi gund bi daweta pismaman,
 
Village by village in the cousins' wedding,

397
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:54,000
şekirê ser serê bûkan.
 
sugar on the heads of the brides.

398
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Hîn li bîra min,
 
Still in my memory,

399
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:58,000
Ew hevalên min,
 
Those friends of mine,

400
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Narez bîra min.
 
I never forget them.

401
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Hemgî bi hev ra dilîstin,
 
We always played together,

402
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:37,000
tûjî û qîlî û çengilî,
 
sharp and loud and jumping,

403
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Seydayê taxtî û çavhelkî,
 
The teacher of the board and clear eyes,

404
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:42,000
